{title: We Have an Anchor}
{artist: Priscilla J. Owens / William J. Kirkpatrick}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: F}
{tempo: 105}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Tabernacle Hymns Number Five (Chicago, Illinois: Tabernacle Publishing, 1955), # 121)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Will your anchor [Bb]hold in the [C]storms of [F]life,
[F]When the [C]clouds unfold their [G7]wings of [C7]strife?
[C7]When the [F]strong tides [C7]lift and the cables [F7]strain,
[F7]Will your anchor [Bb]drift, or [C7]firm re[F]main?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]We have an anchor that keeps the soul
[F]Steadfast and sure while the billows [C]roll,
[F]Fastened to the Rock which [Bb]cannot move,
[C]Grounded firm and deep [Bb]in the [C7]Savior’s [F]love.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]It is safely [Bb]moored, ’twill the [C]storm with[F]stand,
[F]For ’tis [C]well secured by the [G7]Savior’s [C7]hand;
[C7]And the [F]cables, [C7]passed from His heart to [F7]mine,
[F7]Can defy that [Bb]blast, thro’ [C7]strength di[F]vine.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]It will surely [Bb]hold in the [C]Straits of [F]Fear—
[F]When the [C]breakers have told that the [G7]reef is [C7]near;
[C7]Though the [F]tempest [C7]rave and the wild winds [F7]blow,
[F7]Not an angry [Bb]wave shall our [C7]bark o’er[F]flow.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]It will firmly [Bb]hold in the [C]Floods of [F]Death—
[F]When the [C]waters cold chill our [G7]latest [C7]breath,
[C7]On the [F]rising [C7]tide it can never [F7]fail,
[F7]While our hopes a[Bb]bide with[C7]in the [F]Veil.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[F]When our eyes be[Bb]hold through the [C]gath’ring [F]night
[F]The [C]city of gold, our [G7]harbor [C7]bright,
[C7]We shall [F]anchor [C7]fast by the heav’nly [F7]shore,
[F7]With the storms all [Bb]past for[C7]ever[F]more.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
